We demonstrate that the decay width ratios $\Gamma(B	o D\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(B	o D^* \ell ar{
u})$ and $\Gamma(B	o D^* \ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(D^* 	o D\ell ar{
u})$ diverge from the heavy quark limit predictions of $8/3$ and $3/5$, respectively, by substantial margins. These discrepancies are primarily attributed to the significant masses of the $B$ and $D^*$ states. Consequently, these mass effects must be explicitly incorporated into the calculation of the $B	o D(	ext{P})\ell ar{
u}$ decay width.
